abled, disabled and unknown rows; every before-and-after edit state for review, critique and authoring calls; first and resumed authoring turns over every bad carrier; an out-of-lane authoring item; an interrupted launch; and every lane, shared, detached, unclaimed, close-first, spool-write and refused-commit state -> what its chain shows: the finding is answered. Expected now states that a refused record commit is never success, and the edit check's outcomes: an edit told apart from another call's record commit, edits reported, unreadable history as unable to check, and neither a refused nor an unable check ever reported as success -> why it is ready: Expected now claims every arm its Method drives and SR-243's acceptance names. The cases exist, and Full is honest for real git fixtures.\n- [APPROVE] TC-385 -> the obligation: read the coordinator-cycle guidance and its synchronized copies for the required call invocation, blackout refusal, outcome meanings, spool behaviour and the retirement of direct Sol and Terra launch recipes -> what its chain shows: `Verifies` is now SR-243 alone, the row whose acceptance now holds the guidance obligation, so the clause it pins has its home -> why it is ready: an observable text condition with two named, existing cases, and Smoke is honest for a text pin. It verifies an SR directly, which is an honest shape where no LLR decomposes the arm.\n\nOUTCOME: APPROVE rows=4\n\nSITTING: JUDGED kinds=amendment;first-approval\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_018oBgsj3hpjKAeptKB9LSx1","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
