{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user (an unattended coordinator loop) repeatedly launches me as an INDEPENDENT adjudicator for lanes of the ai-template kit repo. Tasks:\n   - **Dispute sittings:** rule each finding FIX, SUCCESSOR, DISMISS (out-of-scope / refuted / not-worth-cost) or ESCALATE, under PROCESS.md §6 \"Review threat model\".\n   - **Amendment sittings:** MEANING vs CLARITY, marking a row `[MEANING+BLESS]` when I would bless it on a released rung.\n   - **First-approval sittings:** APPROVE or RETURN per row, with `## Dispositions` toml drafts for returns.\n   - **Done-when sittings:** CLARITY, BLESSED or SUCCESSOR, with a verbatim digest.\n   - **Disposition sittings:** for partial closes, with a successor drafted in my own spec's `## Dispositions`.\n   - **Act turns:** reattest snapshot, then Status flips plus an approves snapshot, each as its own commit.\n\n   Every verdict goes in exactly one file, with headings `## <kind>`, the machine lines, and a final `SITTING: JUDGED kinds=...`. Each is committed once with trailer `WI: WI-NNN` and `Loop-Session: 20261021T045653Z-213020` in the same final trailer block. Constraints, verbatim in spirit: \"Do not edit the code, the review, the findings file or any registry\"; \"Do NOT edit any registry CELL either way\"; act turns: \"You may not write or edit anything under `docs/reviews/`, edit any registry cell but a listed row's `Status`, or approve or re-attest a row that is not listed\"; \"If the snapshot REFUSES, naming a row that is not listed ... Stop there: commit nothing further, and report the refusal.\" `OWNER_SCRATCHPAD.md` is owner-only: never read, cite or act on it. \"Fail toward RETURN\" / \"Fail toward MEANING.\" \"Judge the CELLS BELOW and nothing else\"; \"an amendment's author is not a witness to their own intent.\"\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - The SN→SR→LLR→TC spine; registries `docs/requirements/{system,low-level}-requirements.toml`, `docs/test/test-cases.toml` (TOML, `[test.TC-###]` etc.); the snapshot `docs/archive/last_approved/` with `acts.toml` (seq entries) and `README.md` log.\n   - Derived-requirement rules (§2(c)): Hat-Refs; Rationale argues the lens; \"fed back to the needs\"; a perspective record (`hats.py record <file> --check --strict`).\n   - Rules applied in returns:\n     - no `shall` in an LLR;\n     - no implementation names in row text;\n     - an AC cannot mint obligations beyond its Requirement;\n     - one decision per row;\n     - a TC Expected must claim the arms it verifies.\n   - Bar-Green attestation, governing_rev walk vs peel, review_attestation 64-commit bound, red-round cap (exit 12), adoption records (LLR-335 and LLR-345), spool-vs-commit for session logs (LLR-269), keep-warm (LLR-270).\n   - Released rung: CLARITY and MEANING+BLESS rows are re-attested by the act turn.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - Verdict files I wrote and committed:\n     - wi-956: 002 (f25567801), 009 (d9087de09), 010 (a706a7810)\n     - wi-962: 003 (b061b98a8)\n     - wi-963: 003 (6de717180), 007 (3d7e66e73)\n     - wi-940: 003 (5bad50dfa), 004 (50cb21ffd)\n     - wi-957: 003 (08afa66b7), 004 (bc728e7f1)\n     - wi-953: 001 (392c84c64), with `docs/work/active/wi-953/WI-953-dispose-the-close-recorded-at.md` gaining a `## Dispositions` toml successor (`supersedes = \"WI-902\"`, title shortened to 111 chars)\n     - wi-958: 005 (24db792b9), 006 (d3b4894de), 009 (f531b944c)\n     - wi-969: 001 (447d66e7e), 006 (4f4944314), 007 (a40196b90)\n     - wi-960: 005 (94c67640f)\n   - Act commits: 34be0f98b, dec3ee790, 7340f1212, e5fdfe6c5, 4eecfc9f2, ed71c0223, 56c0e61f1.\n   - The byte-preserving flip script used in act turns (run with the venv python `-I`):\n     ```python\n     import re\n     plan = {\"docs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml\": [\"LLR-335\",\"LLR-345\"], \"docs/test/test-cases.toml\": [\"TC-360\",\"TC-383\"]}\n     for path, ids in plan.items():\n         lines = open(path,\"rb\").read().split(b\"\\n\")\n         for rid in ids:\n             hdr=[i for i,l in enumerate(lines) if re.match(rb\"^\\[[a-z_]+\\.\"+rid.encode()+rb\"\\]\\s*$\", l)]\n             assert len(hdr)==1\n             i=hdr[0]+1\n             while i<len(lines) and not lines[i].startswith(b\"[\") and not re.match(rb'^status = \"', lines[i]): i+=1\n             assert lines[i].rstrip(b\"\\r\")==b'status = \"Drafted\"'\n             cr=b\"\\r\" if lines[i].endswith(b\"\\r\") else b\"\"\n             lines[i]=b'status = \"Approved\"'+cr\n         open(path,\"wb\").write(b\"\\n\".join(lines))\n     ```\n   - Snapshot commands, run in PowerShell:\n     - `& \"C:\\Projects\\ai-template\\.venv\\Scripts\\python.exe\" project-trajectory/scripts/intake.py snapshot --reattests A,B`\n     - or `... --approves \"reg=WI-NNN;reg=WI-NNN\"` (keep the quotes).\n   - Current lane, WI-960 (`C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-960`):\n     - `docs/plans/WI-960/plan.perspectives.toml` (passes check);\n     - session_service.py, session_keep.py, `scripts/coordinator/codex_call.py`;\n     - tests: `tests/test_session_service.py`, `test_codex_call.py`, `test_codex_call_git.py`, `test_session_keep.py::test_a_keep_warm_ping_from_the_primary_checkout_spools_its_log` (asserts no commit, spool log, HEAD unmoved).\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - **Bash heredoc with nested quotes failed** (\"unexpected EOF\"). Fix: write verdict files with the Write tool, and commit via PowerShell here-strings `@'...'@`.\n   - **`scripts/intake.py` does not exist at the repo root.** Fix: use `project-trajectory/scripts/intake.py`.\n   - **PATH `python` lacks tomllib** (ModuleNotFoundError). Fix: use the venv `C:\\Projects\\ai-template\\.venv\\Scripts\\python.exe`.\n   - **Forgot the SITTING line in one Write (WI-940 003).** Fix: appended it via PowerShell `Add-Content`, then verified there was no CRLF in the committed blob.\n   - **WI-953 successor title was 123 characters, over the 120 limit.** Fix: shortened to 111 characters, verified with `intake.parse_dispositions(text, where)`.\n   - **Miscounted rows in WI-962** (\"six\" vs five). Fix: edited the intro before committing.\n   - **Hook notes on commits:** `format` SKIP (ruff not importable by Python 3.12), and check_trajectory advisory warnings. I reported these, not fixed them.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - I reproduced dispute scenarios with scratch tests in temp dirs, built on the lanes' own test helpers: WI-956 F1 (refuted), WI-963 F1 (confirmed, FIX). For WI-958 F1 I refuted by code trace: the draw gate precedes every draw, the exit-9 park leaves the lane unchanged, and `complete_review_round` clears the marker first.\n   - Consistency across lanes: missing perspective records for derived rows were returned in WI-957, WI-958 and WI-960 and later answered.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - Dispute brief WI-956 (findings F1, governing_rev / empty review carrier).\n   - Combined sitting WI-956 009 (amendment: TC-205, LLR-207, TC-132).\n   - Combined sitting WI-956 010 (amendment re-sit).\n   - Act turn WI-956 (reattest LLR-207, TC-205, TC-132).\n   - Combined sitting WI-962 003 (amendment: LLR-021, TC-021, SR-031, LLR-031, TC-031).\n   - Act turn WI-962.\n   - Combined sitting WI-963 003 (amendment LLR-153, LLR-158; first-approval LLR-342, TC-373).\n   - Dispute WI-963 007 F1.\n   - Sitting WI-940 003 (first-approval TC-374).\n   - Sitting WI-940 004 (re-sit).\n   - Act WI-940.\n   - Sitting WI-957 003 (first-approval SR-241, LLR-341, TC-371, TC-372).\n   - Sitting WI-957 004 (re-sit).\n   - Act WI-957.\n   - Disposition WI-953 (WI-902 partial close, owner route given).\n   - Sitting WI-958 005 (first-approval, 11 rows).\n   - Sitting WI-958 006 (re-sit).\n   - Dispute WI-958 009 F1.\n   - Act WI-958 (11 flips).\n   - Done-when WI-969